#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:2
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:4
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:7
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:9
msgid "To use PyBaMM, you must have Python 3.10 — 3.14 installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:11
msgid ""
"To install Python 3 download the installation files from `Python’s website "
"<https://www.python.org/downloads/windows/>`__. Make sure to tick the box on "
"``Add Python 3.X to PATH``. For more detailed instructions please see the "
"`official Python on Windows guide <https://docs.python.org/3.9/using/windows."
"html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:18
msgid "Install PyBaMM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:21
msgid "User install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:23
msgid ""
"Launch the Command Prompt and go to the directory where you want to install "
"PyBaMM. You can find a reminder of how to navigate the terminal `here "
"<http://www.cs.columbia.edu/~sedwards/classes/2015/1102-fall/"
"Command%20Prompt%20Cheatsheet.pdf>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:27
msgid ""
"We recommend to install PyBaMM within a virtual environment, in order not to "
"alter any distribution python files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:30
msgid "To create a virtual environment within your current directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:34
msgid "uv venv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:38
msgid ""
"This creates a ``.venv`` directory. You can then “activate” the environment "
"using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:40
msgid ".venv\\Scripts\\activate.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:46
msgid "First install ``virtualenv``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:48
msgid "python -m pip install virtualenv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:52
msgid "Then create a virtual environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:54
msgid "python -m virtualenv env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:58
msgid "You can then “activate” the environment using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:60
msgid "env\\Scripts\\activate.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:64
msgid ""
"When you are ready to exit the environment and go back to your original "
"system, just type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:66
msgid "deactivate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:70
msgid "PyBaMM can be installed via ``uv``, ``pip``, or ``conda``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:74
msgid "uv pip install pybamm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:80
msgid "pip install pybamm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:86
msgid "conda install -c conda-forge pybamm-base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:90
msgid "PyBaMM’s :ref:`required dependencies <install-required-dependencies>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:92
msgid ""
"(such as ``numpy``, ``casadi``, etc) will be installed automatically when "
"you install ``pybamm`` using ``pip`` or ``pybamm-base`` using ``conda``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:95
msgid ""
"For an introduction to virtual environments, see (https://realpython.com/"
"python-virtual-environments-a-primer/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:99
msgid "Optional - JaxSolver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:101
msgid "Users can install ``jax`` and ``jaxlib`` to use the Jax solver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:105
msgid "uv pip install \"pybamm[jax]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:111
msgid "pip install \"pybamm[jax]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:115
msgid ""
"This command automatically downloads and installs ``pybamm`` and the "
"compatible versions of ``jax`` and ``jaxlib`` on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:117
msgid ""
"PyBaMM's full `conda-forge distribution <index.rst#installation>`_ "
"(``pybamm``) includes ``jax`` and ``jaxlib`` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:120
msgid "Uninstall PyBaMM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:122
msgid "PyBaMM can be uninstalled by running"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:124
msgid "pip uninstall pybamm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:128
msgid "in your virtual environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:131
msgid "Installation using WSL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/windows.rst:133
msgid ""
"If you want to install the optional PyBaMM solvers, you have to use the "
"Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL). You can find the installation "
"instructions on the `Installation <windows-wsl.rst>`_ page."
msgstr ""
